<http://data.silknow.org/object/b51728ba-0abc-34d2-ab02-4c4ea7e28f08>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Silk panel, France, 1705-1710."@en , "Panel of silk with a yellow ground and a vertical pattern of a parrot regarding a butterfly. The bird is perched on a tree which grows out of a tub and its trunk is intertwined with flowers and various bizarre objects and patterns.\n\nThe pattern is brocaded in pastel coloured silks in mauve, pink and green, enhanced by plain, silver-gilt thread (filé) on a white core and silver gilt frost (frisé) thread on a bright yellow core. The brocading is bound in 1\\4 twill. The pale green of the pattern is created by a patterned weft, the ground is a pale yellow.\n\nThe length is backed with a steel blue tabby silk and is edged with yellow braid which is patterned with plain silver-gilt thread."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/0ed08411-0812-3ab6-a80c-909ed08b8e7b> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Panel of silk with a yellow ground and a vertical pattern of a parrot regarding a butterfly. The bird is perched on a tree which grows out of a tub and its trunk is intertwined with flowers and various bizarre objects and patterns.\n\nThe pattern is brocaded in pastel coloured silks in mauve, pink and green, enhanced by plain, silver-gilt thread (filé) on a white core and silver gilt frost (frisé) thread on a bright yellow core. The brocading is bound in 1\\4 twill. The pale green of the pattern is created by a patterned weft, the ground is a pale yellow.\n\nThe length is backed with a steel blue tabby silk and is edged with yellow braid which is patterned with plain silver-gilt thread."@en , "Silk panel, France, 1705-1710."@en ;
